{"tool_name":"kc-hits","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"kc-hits","home":"https://gitlab.com/i1650/kc-hits.git","license":"MIT","summary":"A tool to aid in the evaluation and classification of chemical carcinogens.","addition_date":"2022-06-28T09:14:53.807753Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:59:44.277521Z","tool_type":["Workflow"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:kc-hits","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"reisfeldb@iarc.fr","name":"Brad Reisfeld","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"name":"kc-hits","operating_system":["Windows"],"owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btac189","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: The evaluation of chemicals for their carcinogenic hazard requires the analysis of a wide range of data and the characterization of these results relative to the key characteristics of carcinogens. The workflow used historically requires many manual steps that are labor-intensive and can introduce errors, bias and inconsistencies. Results: The automation of parts of the evaluation workflow using the kc-hits software has led to significant improvements in process efficiency, as well as more consistent and comprehensive results.","authors":[{"name":"Benbrahim-Tallaa L."},{"name":"De Conti A."},{"name":"El Ghissassi F."},{"name":"Grosse Y."},{"name":"Gwinn W."},{"name":"Reisfeld B."},{"name":"Schubauer-Berigan M."}],"citationCount":7,"date":"2022-05-15T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"kc-hits: A tool to aid in the evaluation and classification of chemical carcinogens"},"pmcid":"PMC9306747","pmid":"35561175"}],"topic":[{"term":"Biochemistry","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3292"},{"term":"Compound libraries and screening","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3343"},{"term":"Toxicology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2840"},{"term":"Workflows","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0769"}],"validated":1},"biosc